>.USD.A: credit from all lenders to households (H), non-financial companies (N), government (G) and all non-financial borrowers (C), break-adjusted, US dollars","note":"Total credit is the loans and debt securities that governments, non-financial companies and households owe to every kind of lender, as the BIS compiles it, converted to US dollars, so a row can move with the currency. Government debt is at market value where the BIS has it and at nominal value otherwise; each row says which. Not split is the BIS total minus the three lines where they do not add up exactly. This already contains the debt securities and bank loans shown elsewhere on this tab, so never add them together. Source: Bank for International Settlements."}